    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.notify\n\n### Description\n\nIt would be nice if there was a `true` by default `enabled` option, which controls whether `vim.notify` is set during `setup()`.\nI am using mini.notify just for it's LSP notifications. My `vim.notify` is handled by another plugin.\nNow that `setup()` overrides `vim.notify` I get inconsistent behavior depending on plugin loading order and whether an LSP is running, since I load mini.notify on `LspAttach`.",
